{
  "description": "The frame's \"Button actions\" rows read out of its event map, and written back (docs/events.md \"Event map\"). Each case is one rule of frame.json `eventMap` (`event_map` on the wire); `expect` is the row it means \u2014 its gesture, its action, the two titles the section shows (a scene named by id is called by its name: the scene `weather` is \"Weather\"), and the rule the row writes back \u2014 or null for a rule the section does not write, which it keeps as it is. Replayed by the SPA (frontend/src/utils/frameEventMap.ts bindingOfRule / bindingRule / frameGestureTitle / frameActionTitle; cloud/apps/auth-web/src/test/shared-spa/button-map-fixtures.test.ts) and the iOS app (ios/FrameOSKit/Sources/FrameOSKit/Contracts/ButtonBindings.swift; ButtonMapFixtureTests.swift).",
